[Avibe Harness] Watch "{name}" was automatically paused because its waiter exited successfully {count} times within {window} seconds. This pattern can create duplicate Agent Runs when a persistent level is reported as a new event on every cycle.

Watch ID: {id}
Successful exit timestamps:
{timestamps}
Latest exit code: 0
Latest stdout:
{stdout}
Latest stderr:
{stderr}

Inspect the Watch with `vibe watch show {id}` and inspect the waiter implementation. Fix it so exit 0 means one new reportable event. While the condition is unchanged or not ready, return one of this Watch's allowed retry exit codes: {retry_codes}. For a completed cycle with nothing reportable, return 64 and print `avibe-watch: no-event` to stderr. A recurring waiter must keep a durable cursor, state transition, or domain cooldown so the same level is not emitted repeatedly.

After an unambiguous, reversible fix, verify the waiter behavior, update the Watch if needed, and resume it with `vibe watch resume {id}`. If the correct fix is uncertain or cannot be verified safely, leave the Watch paused and report the blocker. Do not process the latest stdout as an ordinary event; it was retained as diagnostic evidence for this repair.

